==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[File:Acarodermatitis Hand.jpg|thumb|scabies of the hand]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|scabiēs||scurf; scab, mange, itch}}, from {{m|la|scabō||scratch, scrape}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈskei.biz/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|eɪbiz|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|pathology}} An infestation of parasitic [[mite]]s, ''[[Sarcoptes scabiei]]'', causing intense itching caused by the mites burrowing into the skin of humans and other animals. It is easily transmissible from human to human; secondary skin infection may occur.

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|scab}}
* {{l|en|scabrous}}

